 "authored_by": "firewall-IA project, repo-authored; invented or generic strings",
 "decision": "D58 / spec r3 sections 2.1 and 4.4: benign values that legitimately contain special symbols",
 "min_entries": 150,
 "notes": [
  "Purpose: benign values whose characters overlap attack syntax (' # ! & ; % + < > -- / \") so that the model cannot learn 'special symbol => BLOCK' (spec 2.1, HIGH-evidence family). Values are short non-name texts, surname-only apostrophe names, brand names, product codes, math and recipe fragments.",
  "No real person's full name, no real address, no e-mail address and no URL appears here. The at-sign is not used at all. Brand names are generic trademarks used as ordinary words.",
  "No SQL, shell, markup or script syntax is included (technical prose and code are deferred by D59, spec 2.1). Entries such as 'a<b' or '-- see above' are plain-language or arithmetic uses.",
  "The group 'survival_fixture' holds the five values that MUST survive the benign oracle (spec 4.4): O'Neil, Apt #4, AT&T, 100%, a<b. The builder fails if any of them is not ACCEPTED.",
  "Some values are listed in more than one group (the survival fixture repeats entries of other groups); the builder de-duplicates exact strings and keeps the first occurrence in file order.",
  "Fingerprint risk: the pool is small and hand-written and every entry contains at least one special symbol. Downstream use must mix these with symbol-free values of the same role so that 'has symbol' does not become a benign marker."
 ],
